  "context": {
    "text": "What this study tests: We ran a 12B medical AI model locally on a MacBook Pro (with a full 96k-word working memory, so nothing is cut off) across three types of clinical questions: reconciling conflicting medications and disease stages, looking up past hospital stays and procedures, and knowing when to say 'not in the chart' when asked about records that don't exist. We compared three setups at tight (1k), standard (8k), and full-chart (32k) summary budgets: (1) Direct AI (calling the model directly with the chart and question, without Med Agent Hub), (2) Med Agent Hub with chart-only prompts (citation and abstention rules, but no automated clinical checks), and (3) Med Agent Hub with full clinical rules and the patient relationship graph.",
    "url": "https://openclinai.org/med-agent-hub/wahs-architecture/",
    "label": "How Med Agent Hub works \u2192"
  },
